    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "The function\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}(t,x)=\\langle x,\\,\\text{_____},\\,\\sqrt{7}\\sec t\\rangle\n$$\n\nwith $-\\pi/2<t<\\pi/2$ and $x\\in\\mathbb R$ parametrizes the sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder\n\n$$\n6z^2-7y^2=42,\\qquad z\\ge \\sqrt{7}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the second component of $\\mathbf{f}$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Divide the Cartesian equation by $42$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{z^2}{7}-\\frac{y^2}{6}=1\n$$\n\nThe base curve uses $z$ and $y$; $x$ is the free coordinate. Substituting the supplied component gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^2}{6}=\\frac{(\\sqrt{7}\\sec t)^2}{7}-1=\\sec^2 t-1=\\tan^2 t.\n$$\n\nChoose $y=\\sqrt{6}\\tan t$, which takes every real value on the given interval. This is the positive-tangent orientation used in the choices. The scale is $\\sqrt{6}=\\sqrt{6}$. Thus\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{6}\\tan t,\\qquad \\mathbf{f}(t,x)=\\langle x,\\,\\sqrt{6}\\tan t,\\,\\sqrt{7}\\sec t\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCheck in the normalized equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(\\sqrt{7}\\sec t)^2}{7}-\\frac{(\\sqrt{6}\\tan t)^2}{6}&=\\sec^2 t-\\tan^2 t\\\\&=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe secant coordinate satisfies the positive-sheet condition. The tangent coordinate ranges over all real values, and arbitrary real $x$ extends the base curve along the cylinder axis. Therefore the second component is $\\sqrt{6}\\tan t$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/id": "122851d6-86a6-590b-a408-577c6e3bad5b",
